  "reason": "Each FR-02 requirement maps to an assertion that fails if it is violated. (1) POST /run returns 202 with a run_id: test_fr02.py:103 and :105. Scope write: read key gets 403 at :296, and the write key is accepted at :83. (2) Spawn via create_subprocess_exec with the shlex-split argv, no shell, timeout equal to TASKQ_TASK_TIMEOUT: :128 fails if the spy is never called (shell path), :130 pins args == ('echo','ok'), :134 pins no shell kwarg, :136 pins the wait_for timeout to the 10.0 env value. :317 shows shell metacharacters are not interpreted. (3) State machine: done/failed/timeout end states at :145, :158, :170; legal and illegal transitions at :148-149, :161, :171, :187, :194; the executor rejects pending to done at :359-360; initial pending at :179. Timeout enforcement and no orphan process at :254 and :265. (4) task_results persistence: :204-213 check exit_code, stdout_tail, stderr_tail, duration_ms, finished_at, and that the columns exist. (5) GET /runs: read scope at :76 and :285, history newest first at :230-234 with three distinct run_ids compared against the reversed creation order. Weak spots, none enough to reject: duration_ms >= 0 at :210 is loose but is paired with a non-null check, and the intermediate running state is only covered through is_transition_allowed and executor._set_status.",
